  "summary": "I wrote the cart scene in `src/main.ts`, but I could not confirm it compiles or renders. `@aura3d/engine` is missing from `node_modules/@aura3d` in this sandbox, so `typecheck` can only report \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\" and an implicit-any error on the `onFrame` callback, which follows from the missing module. I wrote against `docs/agents/api-signatures.md` and the recipe sources. The calls I could not confirm are `group(...).rotate(...)` on a group builder and the `Parameters<typeof group>[1][number]` type I use for children.\n\nThe scene is built from primitives only:\n- **Bed:** 10 floor planks with varied length, tone and tilt, plus 4 corner posts and 3 side boards on each of the 4 sides.\n- **Wheels:** 2 wheels on a shared axle. Each has a hub with iron bands, 12 spokes, 12 felloe segments and an iron tyre with nails.\n- **Handles and leg:** 2 rear push handles, a front stretcher, and a two-legged prop stand with a cross bar.\n- **Iron fittings:** bands on the posts, straps and bolts on the end boards, and axle washers and caps.\n- **Cargo:** 4 sacks (one lying across the barrels), 2 barrels with iron hoops, and 2 stacked crates.\n- **Ground:** a dirt plane with darker patches and 16 scattered stones.\n- **Look:** warm lighting with a shadow-casting sun, hemisphere fill, neutral environment and matching fog.\n- **Camera and motion:** a three-quarter view. The whole cart turns slowly and the wheels also spin.\n- **Flags:** after the first drawn frame it sets `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { ready: true, wheelCount: 2, spokeCount: 24, plankCount: 10 }` and `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true`.\n\nTwo things could look wrong in a render. I used the standard right-handed rotation convention for spoke and rim placement, and a flipped sign would misplace them. I also used explicit lights instead of a `looks.preset`, because I couldn't see what the preset would produce.",
